  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and tranquil weather will prevail through the \nweekend.\n\nHigh pressure surface and aloft will remain in place across the Ohio \nValley and eastern Great Lakes through Wednesday night, maintaining \ndry weather and clear skies. Some river valley fog will develop late \ntonight through Wednesday morning across the Southern Tier, and \nagain late Wednesday night through Thursday morning.\n\nA mid level trough will dig southeast across Quebec Thursday, with \nan associated cold front moving southeast across the eastern Great \nLakes. The majority of the height falls and large scale ascent will \nbe displaced well northeast of the area across Quebec, leaving a \nweakly forced and moisture starved cold front crossing our region. \nThis front will bring some increase in cloud cover, but will likely \nmove through dry. Cooler air aloft will bring some increase in lake \ninduced instability, but the lack of synoptic scale moisture will \nlikely only support a few lake effect and upslope clouds.\n\nHigh pressure surface and aloft will build back into the eastern \nGreat Lakes and New England Friday through the weekend with a \ncontinuation of dry weather and sunshine.",
